00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.540
the opponent you guys
 are facing right now...

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.170
...is this guy.

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.670
Why did you tell them?!

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:59.260
<b>Lieutenant Colonel 
Chisato 
Pts: 325,875 
Tokyo Major Land 
Akihabara</b>

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:56.320
Lieutenant Colonel Chisato?!

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:59.260
Never would've guessed 
I was facing you guys.

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:02.650
What is "Chisato"? Your username?

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:04.800
And your avatar has massive boobs! 
Are you secretly an otaku?!

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:06.000
Shut up!

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:08.760
Um, the game's continuing without you.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:12.510
In the final round, you 
can choose your category.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:14.780
Pick the one you're best at.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:17.190
Wow, you're giving us advice?

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.630
It's a free service for new players.

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:19.490
Thanks!

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.570
Do you play this game often?

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:27.620
Yeah. I always keep an eye out for 
good questions, as well as new ones.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:30.450
As long as I remember the 
answer and some keywords,

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:32.630
I can compose lots of questions later.

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:34.700
You go to all that trouble?

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:38.040
Sure do. I'm instantly on top 
of anything related to quiz bowl.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.640
You've gotta be starved of 
questions at all times.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.340
<i>He said that so casually...</i>

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:45.600
<i>That line would sound suffocating 
if Sasajima-senpai said it!</i>

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.170
Aw, they're all taken?

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.530
<b>Please select two categories:

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:54.150
<i>Category selection complete.</i>

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.990
Why did I have to end up facing 
off against them in this game?

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:01.280
Mikuriya-kun's picked 
"Natural Science" and "Lifestyle"?

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:03.850
He's the very definition of a science nerd.

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:06.960
He must have picked "Lifestyle" because 
he thought you two would be bad at it.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:09.110
<i>"Literature" is the obvious choice,</i>

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:11.650
<i>but will the other be "Manga, 
Anime, and Video Games"?</i>

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:13.960
<i>Won't Koshiyama try to 
make this challenging?</i>

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:17.920
<i>He did win some points off of me, 
even if only on a few questions.</i>

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:20.970
<i>I'd rather not have to 
reveal my hand here...</i>

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:23.330
<i>But as long as I'm in this 
showdown, I'll show no mercy!</i>

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:24.970
<b>Huh?</b>

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:25.980
<b>Huh?</b>

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:26.480
<b>Smartphone!</b>

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:26.980
<b>Smartphone!</b>

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:27.230
<b>Uh?</b>

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:27.980
<b>Huh?</b>

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.850
<b>Card Sniping Quiz</b>

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:30.850
<i>Card Sniping Quiz!</i>

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:44.370
<b>Question</b>

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:35.160
<i>The fastest on the draw wins this battle to 
find the correct answer out of several cards!</i>

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:45.490
<b>Incorrect</b>

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:37.610
<b>Incorrect</b>

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.610
<b>Correct</b>

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:39.860
<b>Incorrect</b>

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:44.450
<i>If you make two incorrect 
guesses, you're out!</i>

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:47.250
"Card Sniping"?

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:50.860
There's no fixed number of 
cards or correct answers,

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:53.340
so even if you get one right, 
stay focused right to the end.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:54.060
Right!

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:55.960
You're blabbing too much.

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:59.220
<b>Card Sniping Quiz
Natural Science
Question 1</b>

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:59.220
<b>Which of the following 
numbers is divisible by 3?</b>

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:58.670
A math question?!

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:01.170
N-Not that one, right?

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:03.420
What's with all those digits?!

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:04.850
I don't know... I don't think that one is!

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:09.780
<i>The trick to this one is that the sum 
of all the digits is a multiple of three.</i>

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:11.810
<i>Once you know that, it's 
easy to do it in your head.</i>

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:15.160
Damn! He got that one!

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:16.440
Huh? You knew it?

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:17.650
Yes! Got it!

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:19.840
Wow!

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:21.570
Are you good at mental arithmetic?

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:22.570
<b>Doesn't know
 the trick, but 
worked it out
 in his head</b>

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:22.570
I'm a rank 2 with an abacus!

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:25.130
Okay! Leave the "Manga, Anime, 
and Video Games" one to me!

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:25.780
It's all yours!

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:30.250
<b>Which of the following were game consoles 
released by Sega for home use?</b>

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:31.000
<b>Manga, Anime, and Video Games</b>

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.000
<b>SegaStation</b>

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:33.660
Heh, no such thing.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:34.380
Huh?

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.230
Dreamcast! Yes!

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:35.670
<b>Dreamcast</b>

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:40.460
Are you kidding me?!

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:41.800
He got it first!

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:44.510
Ashiya-san, he's a total otaku, isn't he?!

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:48.020
Well, he's on the quiz team, 
so he's not exactly inexperienced...

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:50.430
<b>Lifestyle</b>

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:50.430
<i>"Lifestyle..."</i>

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.640
<i>What kind of question will it be?</i>

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:55.380
<i>I realize now, after seeing the last question,</i>

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:58.110
<i>that if you guess after seeing the whole 
word on the card, it'll be too late.</i>

00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:02.480
Inoue, think of some possible 
answers before the cards come up.

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:07.300
Why don't we try to collate the answers in 
our heads and match them to the cards?

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:09.370
If we're right, we can buzz in reflexively.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.960
Oh... We might be able 
to buzz in faster that way.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.950
<i>I thought he was just 
a fountain of knowledge,</i>

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:17.450
<i>but he's theoretically analyzed the rules, too.</i>

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:21.420
<b>Lifestyle</b>

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:21.420
<b>Which of the 12 months are 
"long months" with 31 days?</b>

00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:21.420
"Long months"?

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:27.260
January, March, May, July, 
August, October, December...

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:27.260
This should be easy, right?

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:28.710
Wait, they're in English?!

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:30.180
So that's it!

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:31.850
March... That's one!

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:33.110
Got it!

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.440
He's fast!

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:38.840
<i>I guess that would've been too easy, huh?</i>

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:42.540
<i>Just because we came up with that plan 
doesn't mean speed will be enough.</i>

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:43.970
<i>But...</i>

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:45.410
<i>What if I try that?</i>

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:51.080
Another one to Mikuriya?!

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:57.670
<i>It's not over yet!</i>

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.510
No letters are even showing yet!

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:05.470
May? It's May!

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:07.210
The plan worked!

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:08.930
"Plan"?! That wasn't a guess?!

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:13.680
<b>The 
End</b>

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:13.680
Nope. I'd decided that if it took a while 
for any letters to show, I'd buzz in.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:16.310
I see now! The number of letters!

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:20.560
May's the only month with only 
three letters in its name.

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:22.400
The fact that it has the fewest letters

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:25.690
means the part of the card where 
the hint isn't visible is much larger.

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:26.820
Oh!

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:29.630
So not seeing the hint 
is a hint in itself?

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:30.660
Right!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:34.410
<i>How did he notice that
loophole in the rules so quickly?</i>

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:38.130
It's pretty amazing to actually 
guess correctly like that.

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:40.840
Interesting.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:43.850
Okay! That just leaves "Literature"!

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:44.530
Yeah!

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:50.300
Very interesting.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:53.520
<b>Literature</b>

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:53.520
<b>Which of the following
 Shakespeare plays is 
counted among the
 "Four Great Tragedies"?</b>

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:55.640
All right! This is easy to narrow down!

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:56.890
I won't lose this one!

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:59.610
Oh, I'm good at these.

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:04.150
<b>A Midsummer Night's Dream
Romeo and Juliet</b>

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:04.150
He got it wrong?

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:07.860
Sorry. See, all the machines 
for this game are taken.

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:11.580
Should middle school kids 
even be in an arcade?

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:13.040
Mikuriya, stop.

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:19.480
Excuse me, but those two are with us. 
Could you see your way to leaving them alone?

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:21.380
We'll give you our machine.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:22.880
Come on over here, you two.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.600
Ashiya-san!

00:14:25.310 --> 00:14:26.630
Oh, cool. One's open now.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.130
Thanks, man.

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:32.760
Let it go. If you start trouble and 
get reported, we'll have a real problem.

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:36.520
What the h—

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:38.740
Huh?

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:42.430
I was next in line.

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:44.270
I don't think you two understand etiquette,

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:46.580
you sad old men.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.780
What did ya call us, you cosplaying bitch?!

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:49.860
You wanna fight us?!

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:53.740
Sure. If we're going to have 
a match, let's do it for real.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.450
A match?

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:59.900
If you guys win, I'll give 
you anything you want.

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:03.200
<i>If</i> you win, that is.

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:04.900
All right!

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.460
Don't forget you said that!

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.520
Which game do you wanna play?!

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:11.100
Pick whichever one you're best at.

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:12.050
Say what?

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:15.180
This is probably a good 
time to get out of here.

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:19.060
But we haven't thanked that 
person for helping us...

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:22.040
I wouldn't call that "helping us."

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:25.470
It doesn't look like that 
was the intention, anyway.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:27.030
A fighting game?

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:34.990
Instakill!

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:37.080
Seriously?

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:38.190
Aw crap!

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:42.710
Aw man, they ran away.

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:45.790
They were all talk, after all. 
Whatever, I'll let them go this time.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:52.950
U-Um, thank you for helping—

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:54.910
I watched you guys playing.

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:55.470
Huh?

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:58.470
It was exciting! You're good at quizzing!

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:00.980
I'd love to play with you guys, too.

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:03.640
You're welcome to play, 
too, Lieutenant Colonel.

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:06.430
You seem to have a bit 
more of an edge at this.

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:09.780
Sorry, but we have to get going.

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:11.620
Let's go, Koshiyama-kun.

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:12.610
R-Right!

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:14.490
Whoa, wait a sec!

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.950
Hey...

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:19.720
Are you guys...

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:21.910
actual quiz freaks?

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:24.920
You take quiz bowl seriously, right?

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.420
Like, keeping an eye out for 
questions and stuff like that?

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.460
You're really going all out!

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:34.340
I bet you spend every day cramming 
just for quiz bowl, right?

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:37.350
Are you honor students at school, too?

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:41.470
Are you making fun of us?

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:42.270
Huh?

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:46.260
I don't care what you say about me.

00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:49.200
I'm used to it.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:50.840
But...

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:54.870
Is it wrong to go all out 
for something you enjoy?

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:56.620
Is it something you should 
get laughed at for?

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:59.620
It just means you like it, that's all!

00:17:00.140 --> 00:17:04.620
Is there something wrong 
with being quiz freaks?!

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:14.340
Let's go, Koshiyama!

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:16.800
Oh... right.

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:24.040
Koshiyama...

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:29.690
I-I'm sorry! I said too much...

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:31.960
Nah, it actually brought a smile to my face.

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:35.400
It means you're really 
into quiz bowl, right?

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:38.590
I'm glad to have new kindred spirits.

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:42.820
Yeah.

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:50.910
What the heck was with that chick, though?

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:52.590
Were those wings I saw?

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:56.220
Yeah! I know this is Akiba, 
but that's just insane, right?

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:58.480
We're holding a quiz event!

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:03.810
<b>Open: 11:00 AM ~

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:03.810
Meow    Meow

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:02.720
What's our store's special attraction today?

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:04.320
"Janken"?

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:07.060
Ding-ding! You're corre—

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:14.980
F-Fukami-san?!

00:18:17.790 --> 00:18:19.850
Maids?! Animal ears?!

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:20.870
M-Maririn...

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:21.990
Oh?

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:24.700
Sasajima-senpai!

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:25.980
Hey.

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:27.260
Hello.

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:32.230
A-All right! As we're here, let's go 
check out Fukami-san's maid café!

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:34.750
Hey, that sounds like heaps of fun!

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:36.130
Please don't!

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:38.860
Come on, Maririn. Back to work, okay?

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:42.160
Okay, we'll show you the way!

00:18:44.610 --> 00:18:48.180
M-Mikuriya-kun, you're going home? 
Why don't you come with us?

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:49.850
Like hell I will.

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:51.530
U-Um...

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:52.820
What?

00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:54.780
Well, um...

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:57.780
If it's okay with you, 
can we exchange contact info?

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:00.740
Huh?

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:02.670
Why?

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:04.100
Why? Because...

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:08.460
Um, I had a lot of fun today, 
s-so I was hoping we could be friends.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:10.420
What kind of idiot are you?

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:12.880
And I'm not your friend.

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:19.130
More importantly, don't forget 
about the regular meet.

00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:26.370
"Regular meet"?

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.730
It's a regularly scheduled competition where

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:31.720
quiz teams from several
schools come together.

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:35.620
It's basically a joint quiz meet.

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:38.320
A quiz meet?

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.690
What's so important about 
the regular meet?

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:44.430
Mikuriya-kun said he'd 
get his revenge there.

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:48.290
A declaration of war, huh? Sounds good.

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:52.560
Well, that means you have 
a rival, doesn't it?

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:56.240
A... rival?

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:57.280
Yep.

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:04.400
S-Sorry!

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:06.120
I'm going home!

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:07.060
Koshiyama-kun?

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:15.540
Chisato-kun!

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:16.940
<b>Lieutenant Colonel Chisato 
Mikuriya Chisato 
Mikuriya Prefectural High School,
First-year</b>

00:20:15.970 --> 00:20:16.940
What?

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:20.140
Why did you go and say something like that?

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:21.900
Don't you feel bad for Koshiyama-kun?

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:25.370
If he got serious, he could
 become a lot better.

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:29.330
That's why I don't want to get 
chummy. I won't show any mercy.

00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:33.290
Well, I look forward to next 
month's regular meet, then.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:36.510
But Koshiyama won't be your only opponent.

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:39.250
In fact, there'll be plenty of 
others who are much tougher.

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:41.130
I'll be competing, too.

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:47.100
No matter who I face, I'll show no 
mercy when I'm laying the smack down.

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:33.700
We saw a new quiz format today: the 
single question with multiple answers.

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:37.330
<b>Single Question 
with Multiple Answers</b>

00:22:34.220 --> 00:22:37.330
They demand broader knowledge 
than questions with only one answer.

00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:39.780
Those were hard...

00:22:39.780 --> 00:22:42.840
But if we get lots of them right, 
we can get lots of points!

00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:45.570
Now, here's a question 
with multiple answers!

